[b]Theys Gone[/b] is an experimental two-player co-op mod for [i]Days Gone[/i] on PC. A guest joins the host's save and helps with the host's missions: they see each other, ride together and fight the host's enemies, while story progress stays on the host's save. This is [b]not full campaign co-op[/b]: each player runs their own copy of the game, and the guest catches up at the host's saves rather than sharing missions live.

I just made this because I wanted to join my wife's sessions and drive around together.

The mod is unofficial and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Bend Studio, Sony Interactive Entertainment or the game's publishers.

[b]Main features[/b]

[list]
[*]Native CO-OP menus for hosting and joining over Steam or LAN.
[*]See your partner's character, animations, held item and motorcycle.
[*]Ride as a passenger on your partner's motorcycle (experimental).
[*]Play on the host's save: the guest loads a copy of it and is reloaded onto the host's later story saves.
[*]Shared enemies: the host's enemies appear for the guest, and the guest's hits count.
[*]Time of day and weather follow the host.
[*]Appearance colors, opt-in friendly fire and teleport to partner in the F8 menu.
[/list]

[b]Experimental:[/b] free roam ([i]FreeRoam=1[/i] on both PCs) lets players split up and simulate enemies in their own regions. It is outside the main use case, and guest-owned enemies attacking the host after regrouping are unproven.

[b]Key limitations[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Back up your saves.[/b] If the guest's save sandbox cannot start, the guest leaves the session ([i]Join blocked[/i]). This check is new; after joining, confirm TheysGone.log shows [i]save guard: guest save sandbox active until restart[/i].
[*]Missions, inventory, loot, doors and camp NPCs are not shared live. Optional objective sync ([i]MissionObjectiveSync=1[/i]) only shares completed objectives; starting and completing jobs still waits for the host's next save.
[*]At most 16 nearby enemy and companion pawns are shared, so hordes are incomplete. Enemy melee damage is estimated; aimed combat and ranged enemies need more testing.
[*]Motorcycle physics, fuel, damage and upgrades are not shared. Your partner uses your outfit model with their colors.
[*]LAN play is unauthenticated and unencrypted: use it only on a trusted network and never forward its port. Steam sessions are encrypted by Steam, but host-save transfer, invite acceptance and Internet/NAT traversal over Steam remain unverified.
[/list]

[b]Requirements[/b]

[list]
[*]The Steam version of [i]Days Gone[/i], build [b]19221447[/b]. The mod disables itself on any other build.
[*]Ultimate ASI Loader (x64).
[*]Windows, or Linux/Steam Deck with Proton. Proton has been tested; native Windows has not.
[*]Both players on the same mod version. Releases that change the network protocol cannot connect to older ones.
[/list]

[b]Installation[/b]

Install on [b]both PCs[/b]. Use [b]Manual Download[/b]; Vortex installation is not supported.

[list]
[*]Back up your saves.
[*]Put Ultimate ASI Loader's [i]version.dll[/i] in [i]BendGame/Binaries/Win64[/i], next to [i]DaysGone.exe[/i]. Don't overwrite an existing loader.
[*]Copy [i]TheysGone.asi[/i] and [i]TheysGone.ini[/i] from the archive into that same folder.
[*]Optional: copy [i]BendGame/Content/Paks/pakchunk99-TheysGone_Brand_P.pak[/i] into the matching game folder for the Theys Gone logos.
[*]On Linux or Steam Deck, set the launch options to [code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="version=n,b" %command%[/code]
[/list]

Then open [b]CO-OP[/b] in the title or pause menu. On Steam, host as invite-only, friends-only or public; your friend uses [b]JOIN A FRIEND[/b], [b]FIND PUBLIC GAMES[/b] or a Steam invite. On LAN, choose [b]HOST LAN GAME[/b] and [b]JOIN LAN GAME[/b], and allow inbound UDP 27777 on the host. Press [b]F8[/b] (gamepad: View/Back + Y) for gameplay settings. Settings are also in [i]TheysGone.ini[/i], except friendly fire, which both players must enable each session.

Upgrading from [i]Days Gone Together[/i]: delete the old [i]DaysGoneTogether.*[/i] files first; old and new versions cannot connect.

[b]More information[/b]

[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/DrSkunk/theys-gone]GitHub README[/url]: full setup, controls, settings and troubleshooting.
[*][url=https://github.com/DrSkunk/theys-gone/blob/main/docs/COOP-ROADMAP.md]Co-op roadmap[/url]: what has been tested and what comes next.
[/list]

[b]Shout outs[/b]

Thanks to the [b]Ultimate ASI Loader[/b] and [b]Dear ImGui[/b] projects, and to the Days Gone modding community.

AI coding assistants were used in development, including for code, reverse-engineering analysis and documentation. The project was directed by a human and tested in the game on real hardware.
